// Update: wasm proc macros expand in a session per calling crate only when they keep state (#908, PR #918, after #830), in
// v0.20261028.3. Canary. Extends lesson 3: most expansions stay kept; the few that remember are run in order.
site {
  updates {
    "stateful-macros" : Page {
      Narrow
      Update: {"2026-10-28", "0.20261028.3", "Macros that remember things between expansions now work, and the rest stay kept.", "session"}
      (InTheme, themes.canary)
      (Requires, site.learn.macros)
      Title: {"Macros that keep state"}
      Description: {"Update to lesson 3: proc macros that keep state between expansions run in a session per crate; the rest stay kept."}

      Step remember("Some macros remember") {
        P pure("Most derives are pure: same input, same output. A few keep state between expansions in a crate: napi-rs registers each constructor it sees, and a later expansion reads the list.")
        P lost("Expand each one in a fresh instance, as lesson 3 did, and that list is lost.")
      }

      Step watch("blaze watches the memory") {
        P count("The macro's allocator counts the bytes still in use. An expansion that leaves some behind marks its module stateful, in blaze's store.")
        P kept("A module that never does (`serde_derive`, `thiserror`, most derives) keeps a fresh instance per expansion, and its expansions stay kept.")
      }

      Step session("A session per crate") {
        P order("A stateful module expands in one session per calling crate, in order, so its state is there when it is read. A module not seen yet expands in a session until a build has run it.")
      }

      Step leftover("Bytes left behind") {
        Quiz q(prompt: "A derive's expansion returns, and leaves 2 KB of memory in use. What does blaze do with that macro from then on?") {
          Choice keep("Keeps each expansion, as it does for `serde_derive`.", "Only a module whose expansions leave nothing behind is expanded fresh and kept.")
          Choice session("Expands it in one session per calling crate.", "Memory left behind means it may remember, so the later expansions in a crate must see it.") {
            Right
          }
          Choice refuse("Refuses to build with it.", "blaze builds with it; it just can't treat each expansion on its own.")
        }
      }

      Step source("Where it comes from") {
        Dim where("In canary since v0.20261028.3 ([#918](https://github.com/indexable-inc/blaze/pull/918) for [#908](https://github.com/indexable-inc/blaze/issues/908), after [#830](https://github.com/indexable-inc/blaze/pull/830)).")
      }
    }
  }
}
